[I] A compact multilingual text to speech synthesis engine

[T] ESpeak is a compact text to speech engine for good quality English and
[T] other languages. Its clear articulation and good intonation makes it
[T] suitable for listening to long text articles. It can speak text files
[T] from the command line, and also operates as a &amp;quot;talker&amp;quot;
[T] within the KDE TTS system as an alternative to Festival etc.

[U] https://espeak.sourceforge.net

[A] jonsd <jsdsf@jsd.clara.co.uk>
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/multimedia
[F] CROSS OBJDIR

[L] GPL
[V] 1.52.0
[P] X ?----5---9

[D] 42cca072aa08ca81c44560d61bfcc67568ad7f00265c458b2baf7d85 espeak-1.52.0.zip https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng/archive/1.52.0/
[D] 991a6e58ae222890b1e74b7662f29012c08f1c2d59def9b3ac8c65e3 sonic-fbf75c3.tar.gz https://github.com/waywardgeek/sonic/archive/fbf75c3d6d846bad3bb3d456cbc5d07d9fd8c104/

[ "$SDECFG_STATIC" = 1 ] || var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON

atstage cross && var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DESPEAK_NG_HOST=espeak-ng

# bundled libsonic from [D] instead of a build time git download
hook_add preconf 3 "tar xf $archdir/sonic-fbf75c3.tar.gz -C $builddir"
var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DFETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_SONIC-GIT=$builddir/sonic-fbf75c3d6d846bad3bb3d456cbc5d07d9fd8c104
var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON
